---
import CaseStudyLayout from '../../layouts/CaseStudyLayout.astro';
import { Picture } from 'astro:assets';
import caseImageVinted01 from '../../assets/case-image-vinted-01.png';
import caseImageVinted02 from '../../assets/case-image-vinted-02.png';
import caseImageVinted03 from '../../assets/case-image-vinted-03.png';
import caseImageVinted04 from '../../assets/case-image-vinted-04.png';
---

<CaseStudyLayout
  title="Enabling Escrow Trading in Poland, a Freshly Monetized Market"
  summary="Designing solutions in payments domain at Vinted as a product designer in a high-growth startup, enabling escrow-based payments in the Polish market for millions."
  role="Product Designer"
  timeline="2019 - 2020"
  platform="Web & Mobile"
>
  <!-- OVERVIEW -->
  <section class="fade-in group border-t border-white/5 pt-12 anim-delay-2">
    <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-8 md:gap-24">
      <div class="md:w-48 shrink-0 pt-1">
        <span class="text-xs font-medium text-[#787885] uppercase tracking-wider">Overview</span>
      </div>
      <div class="w-full space-y-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium text-[#EDEDED] tracking-tight">Executive summary</h2>
        <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-[#A1A1AA] max-w-3xl">
          In 2019, Vinted prepared to launch escrow-based payments in Poland, a market that had
          previously relied on manual transactions. This required collecting users’ full legal names
          to meet payment compliance requirements, data that most Polish users had never been asked
          to provide.
        </p>
        <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-[#A1A1AA] max-w-3xl">
          Over a two-month period, a phased, low-friction data collection strategy was designed and
          launched across new and existing users. The solution resulted in a significant increase in
          full-name submissions and confirmations, with no measurable negative impact on sign-up
          conversion. By the end of the grace period, the majority of active traders were enabled to
          use escrow services, allowing Poland to transition into a monetized market with minimal
          disruption.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SITUATION -->
  <section class="fade-in group border-t border-white/5 pt-12 anim-delay-3">
    <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-8 md:gap-24">
      <div class="md:w-48 shrink-0 pt-1">
        <span class="text-xs font-medium text-[#787885] uppercase tracking-wider">Situation</span>
      </div>
      <div class="w-full space-y-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium text-[#EDEDED] tracking-tight">Context & Problem</h2>
        <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-[#A1A1AA] max-w-3xl">
          Before monetization, Polish users could trade only through manual agreements, handling
          payments and shipping independently and relying entirely on mutual trust. With the
          introduction of escrow services, Vinted’s payment provider was legally required to know
          users’ full legal names before enabling transactions.
        </p>
        <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-[#A1A1AA] max-w-3xl">However:</p>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-[16px] text-[#A1A1AA] list-disc pl-5 marker:text-[#787885]">
          <li>Polish users were not previously required to provide full names</li>
          <li>Many existing users had incomplete, incorrect, or unverified names</li>
          <li>Some users relied on social media sign-ups where names were not necessarily real</li>
          <li>Without compliant data, users would be blocked from trading after launch</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-[#A1A1AA] max-w-3xl">
          The timeline was tight, and a failed rollout risked excluding a large portion of the user
          base from escrow-enabled trade.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-8">
          <Picture
            src={caseImageVinted01}
            alt="Vinted case study - Situation"
            formats={['avif', 'webp']}
            fallbackFormat="png"
            widths={[472, 944]}
            sizes="(min-width: 768px) 944px, 100vw"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            pictureAttributes={{ class: 'block' }}
            class="w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/5 shadow-lg"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- TASK -->
  <section class="fade-in group border-t border-white/5 pt-12 anim-delay-4">
    <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-8 md:gap-24">
      <div class="md:w-48 shrink-0 pt-1">
        <span class="text-xs font-medium text-[#787885] uppercase tracking-wider">Task</span>
      </div>
      <div class="w-full space-y-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium text-[#EDEDED] tracking-tight">Goals & Objectives</h2>
        <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-[#A1A1AA] max-w-3xl">
          The primary objective was to enable escrow-based trading for as many users as possible
          while minimizing friction and negative impact on user behavior.
        </p>
        <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-[#A1A1AA] max-w-3xl">Key goals included:</p>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-[16px] text-[#A1A1AA] list-disc pl-5 marker:text-[#787885]">
          <li>Collect compliant full names from both new and existing users</li>
          <li>Maintaining sign-up and trading conversion rates</li>
          <li>Preserving user trust around privacy and data security</li>
          <li>Supporting a time-bound, legally constrained launch</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-[#A1A1AA] max-w-3xl">
          I led the design of the full-name collection solution, working closely with product,
          engineering, analytics, research, legal, and communications teams.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-8">
          <Picture
            src={caseImageVinted02}
            alt="Vinted case study - Task"
            formats={['avif', 'webp']}
            fallbackFormat="png"
            widths={[472, 944]}
            sizes="(min-width: 768px) 944px, 100vw"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            pictureAttributes={{ class: 'block' }}
            class="w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/5 shadow-lg"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ACTION -->
  <section class="fade-in group border-t border-white/5 pt-12 anim-delay-4">
    <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-8 md:gap-24">
      <div class="md:w-48 shrink-0 pt-1">
        <span class="text-xs font-medium text-[#787885] uppercase tracking-wider">Action</span>
      </div>
      <div class="w-full space-y-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium text-[#EDEDED] tracking-tight">Process & Solution</h2>
        <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-[#A1A1AA] max-w-3xl">
          A Lean UX approach was applied, focusing on iterative design, early validation, and
          data-driven decision-making.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-[15px] font-medium text-[#EDEDED]">User and problem analysis</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-[16px] text-[#A1A1AA] list-disc pl-5 marker:text-[#787885]">
          <li>Segmented users by activity level, trading role, and name status</li>
          <li>Identified critical risk groups, such as active sellers without compliant names</li>
          <li>Mapped existing user flows to uncover friction points</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-[15px] font-medium text-[#EDEDED] mt-4">Hypothesis-driven strategy</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-[16px] text-[#A1A1AA] list-disc pl-5 marker:text-[#787885]">
          <li>New users would be more willing to share personal data during sign-up</li>
          <li>Existing users would comply if given transparency, value context, and time</li>
          <li>Phased communication would reduce backlash and resistance</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-[15px] font-medium text-[#EDEDED] mt-4">Solutions for new users</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-[16px] text-[#A1A1AA] list-disc pl-5 marker:text-[#787885]">
          <li>Added a Full name field to email sign-up forms with clear privacy reassurance</li>
          <li>
            Introduced a confirmation step for Facebook and Google sign-ups, allowing users to
            correct imported names
          </li>
          <li>Tested changes incrementally with close monitoring of registration metrics</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-[15px] font-medium text-[#EDEDED] mt-4">Solutions for existing users</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-[16px] text-[#A1A1AA] list-disc pl-5 marker:text-[#787885]">
          <li>Designed a multi-phase rollout</li>
          <li>Pre-launch communication explaining the upcoming escrow service and its value</li>
          <li>Soft collection via non-disruptive banners and flexible modal prompts</li>
          <li>Grace period collection during first escrow transactions</li>
          <li>Hard collection as a last resort, temporarily hiding items until compliance</li>
          <li>Collaborated with communications to align product UI and messaging</li>
          <li>Conducted guerrilla usability testing to validate clarity and non-disruptiveness</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-[15px] font-medium text-[#EDEDED] mt-4">Delivery and monitoring</h3>
        <ul class="space-y-2 text-[16px] text-[#A1A1AA] list-disc pl-5 marker:text-[#787885]">
          <li>Ensured clear design handoff and close collaboration with developers</li>
          <li>Tracked conversion, submission, and confirmation rates throughout rollout</li>
          <li>Adjusted copy and accessibility based on early feedback</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="mt-8">
          <Picture
            src={caseImageVinted03}
            alt="Vinted case study - Action"
            formats={['avif', 'webp']}
            fallbackFormat="png"
            widths={[472, 944]}
            sizes="(min-width: 768px) 944px, 100vw"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            pictureAttributes={{ class: 'block' }}
            class="w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/5 shadow-lg"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- RESULT -->
  <section class="fade-in group border-t border-white/5 pt-12 anim-delay-5">
    <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row gap-8 md:gap-24">
      <div class="md:w-48 shrink-0 pt-1">
        <span class="text-xs font-medium text-[#787885] uppercase tracking-wider">Result</span>
      </div>
      <div class="w-full space-y-8">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-medium text-[#EDEDED] tracking-tight">Outcome & impact</h2>
        <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-[#A1A1AA] max-w-3xl">
          The phased approach successfully transitioned Poland into a monetized market with
          escrow-based trading.
        </p>
        <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-[#A1A1AA] max-w-3xl">Key outcomes:</p>
        <ul class="space-y-3 text-[16px] text-[#A1A1AA]">
          <li class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#EDEDED]"></span><span
              >Significant increase in full-name submissions and confirmations</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#EDEDED]"></span><span
              >No significant drop in sign-up or engagement metrics</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#EDEDED]"></span><span
              >Majority of active traders enabled for escrow by the end of the grace period</span
            >
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-[#EDEDED]"></span><span
              >Minimal user backlash due to transparent communication and gradual enforcement</span
            >
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-[#A1A1AA] max-w-3xl">
          The project met its primary goal of enabling secure, compliant trade at scale while
          preserving user trust and platform stability.
        </p>

        <div class="mt-8">
          <Picture
            src={caseImageVinted04}
            alt="Vinted case study - Result"
            formats={['avif', 'webp']}
            fallbackFormat="png"
            widths={[472, 944]}
            sizes="(min-width: 768px) 944px, 100vw"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            pictureAttributes={{ class: 'block' }}
            class="w-full rounded-2xl border border-white/5 shadow-lg"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</CaseStudyLayout>
